<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42843" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρώτ-ημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that which is asked, question,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.54
			</span></i>, etc. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ πρὸς τὸ ἐ.
			ἀπόκρισις</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				60
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐ. τοῦ ξυνθήματος</span>
			<i>asking for</i> the password, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				7.44
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					336d
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐρέσθαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				42e
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διπλᾶ ἔστρεφε τὰ -ήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Euthd.</u>
					276d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in Stoic
			terminology, a question requiring the answer 'Yes' or 'No', opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πύσμα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				2.61
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in
			Dialectic, <i>question inviting an answer which may help to refute
				an opponent,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APr.</u>
				64a36
			</span></i>(pl.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				0.77a36
			</span></i>, al.</div>
